 4513: /* Native scroll-driven reveal path DELETED (redesign Wave 0, 2026-08-30).
 4514:  * The @supports (animation-timeline: view()) block that lived here won in
 4515:  * every modern browser and permanently resolved all 24 .cw-reveal elements
 4516:  * to their END state â€” the reveal never played for anyone, ever (verified
 4517:  * on production with Playwright at reduce AND no-preference; see
 4518:  * .planning/DEFECT-reveal-system-2026-08-29.md). The IntersectionObserver
 4519:  * path below is now the ONE reveal system. If the native path returns, it
 4520:  * must ship with a measured probe of the overridden state in a real
 4521:  * browser, per the DEFECT doc's gate. */
 4522: 
 4523: /* Generic reveal â€” observed by ScrollReveal client component.
 4524:  *
 4525:  * Progressive enhancement: baseline is VISIBLE so no-JS clients and
 4526:  * fullPage screenshots see the content. ScrollReveal adds the
 4527:  * .cw-js-reveals class to [data-mode="cw"] on mount; only then do
 4528:  * the hidden state and the transition apply. This avoids the
 4529:  * "blank fullPage screenshot" bug we hit on the foyer routes. */
 4530: [data-mode="cw"] .cw-reveal {
 4531:   opacity: 1;
 4532:   transform: none;
 4533:   transition:
 4534:     /* Wave 0: 0.9s -> 0.55s. Now that the reveal actually RUNS (the dead
 4535:        native path above is deleted), 0.9s reads as syrup at scroll speed;
 4536:        0.55s with the same ease finishes inside one scroll gesture. */
 4537:     opacity 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
 4538:     transform 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
 4539: }
 4540: [data-mode="cw"].cw-js-reveals .cw-reveal:not(.is-in) {
 4541:   opacity: 0;
 4542:   transform: translateY(40px);
 4543: }
 4544: [data-mode="cw"] .cw-reveal.is-in {
 4545:   opacity: 1;
 4546:   transform: none;
 4547: }
